  "notes": "GAAP SID. Receipts/disbursements from p4 Total Governmental Funds column. Ending cash = cash on deposit with County Treasurer (p3); investments 100,000 shown separately. Payment of warrants (291,180) is other financing, p4. Balance sheet is the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1); warrants issued not registered (no due-date split) put in debt due in more than one year per the SID rule. Detail uses the budgetary-basis Actual column of the budget schedules (pp5-6), which differs from GAAP statement (e.g. GF taxes 222,199 vs 245,893); the 11,959 GF payment of warrants is positive as printed. Functions for SID expenses listed by object are mapped to general government (maintenance, collection, engineering) with debt costs as debt service. State motor vehicle allocation/homestead/credits treated as state aid. No business-type funds, no transfers. Read pages 1-6 of 6"
}
